 <class>GridCalculatorDialog</class>
 <widget class="QDialog" name="GridCalculatorDialog">
  <property name="geometry">
   <rect>
    <x>0</x>
    <y>0</y>
    <width>820</width>
    <height>300</height>
   </rect>
  </property>
  <property name="windowTitle">
   <string>Grid calculator</string>
  </property>
  <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="mainVerticalLayout">
   <property name="spacing">
    <number>8</number>
   </property>
   <property name="margin" stdset="0">
    <number>8</number>
   </property>
   <item>
    <widget class="QPlainTextEdit" name="edit_command">
     <property name="minimumSize">
      <size>
       <width>0</width>
       <height>62</height>
      </size>
     </property>
     <property name="maximumSize">
      <size>
       <width>16777215</width>
       <height>80</height>
      </size>
     </property>
     <property name="toolTip">
      <string>&lt;html&gt;The expression to evaluate. Write a grid by its name, as shown&lt;br&gt;in the list below (double-click a name to insert it) - blanks&lt;br&gt;and all. Everything else is plain arithmetic: + - * / ^ ( )&lt;br&gt;and the functions on the right. A grid whose name is also a&lt;br&gt;function name (abs, log, ...) must be written &amp;name.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Comparisons &amp;lt; &amp;lt;= &amp;gt; &amp;gt;= on grids give a MASK (true/false per node);&lt;br&gt;== and != compare two grids or two masks. Masks combine with&lt;br&gt;&amp;amp; | ! xor; put each comparison in parentheses: (a &amp;gt; 1) &amp;amp; (b &amp;lt; 2).&lt;br&gt;In arithmetic a mask counts as 0/1. Wrong operands are refused&lt;br&gt;before anything is computed.&lt;/html&gt;</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
